{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Speak to the children of Israel and say to them, When you come into the land</b> — Because He introduces here, for each one of the festivals, a new commandment in addition to the cessation of labor and the sacred convocation, each festival is set apart as a separate pericope in which He admonishes, \"Speak to the children of Israel.\" And since the festival of Shavuot's date depends on the Omer, He said everything in one pericope. And because the Day of Remembrance (Rosh HaShanah) and the Day of Atonement (Yom Kippur) are in one month and both are of one theme — the matter of sins and their atonement for the penitents — He did not say for the Day of Atonement, \"Speak to the children of Israel,\" since the first admonition suffices for it, and He made of them two pericopes because they are distinct subjects:" "And the sense of <b>And you shall reap its harvest</b> is that you shall not reap any harvest in the land until you reap the Omer and bring it as the first of your harvest to the priest. And likewise, \"From the time the sickle begins among the standing grain you shall begin to count\" (Deuteronomy 16:9) — from when you begin with a sickle on any standing grain, for it is forbidden to wave a sickle over the standing grain until the day on which you begin to count:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:58:15.201801352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}